  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#the-htmloptionscollection-interface\n\n> Returns the item with ID or name name from the collection.\n\nThis text refers to `HTMLOptionsCollection`, which is a collection of `option` elements. It says that `namedItem` returns an element if it has a matching `id` or`name`. However, `option` elements are not documented as supporting the `name` attribute. As a result, browsers are inconsistent in their implementation of `namedItem`: Firefox 42 will return an element that has a matching name, but IE 11 will not.\n",
